# camera-creds.env — Reolink camera identity + RTSP URLs
#
# Format: one block per camera (CAM1..CAM6). Each block needs:
#   CAM{N}_IP          — LAN IP of the camera
#   CAM{N}_HTTP_USER   — HTTP API username (default "admin")
#   CAM{N}_HTTP_PASS   — HTTP API password
#   CAM{N}_RTSP_URL    — full RTSP URL including user/pass/stream path
#
# The IP/USER/PASS can be omitted if you embed everything in RTSP_URL.
# Both forms are accepted; both must point at the same camera.
#
# This file MUST NOT be committed — it's in .gitignore.
# Copy this template to camera-creds.env and fill in your values.

# === CAM1 — example: Front door ===
# CAM1_IP=192.168.1.21
# CAM1_HTTP_USER=admin
# CAM1_HTTP_PASS=your-camera-password
# CAM1_RTSP_URL=rtsp://admin:your-camera-password@192.168.1.21:554/h264Preview_01_main

# === CAM2 — example: Back yard ===
# CAM2_IP=192.168.1.22
# CAM2_HTTP_USER=admin
# CAM2_HTTP_PASS=your-camera-password
# CAM2_RTSP_URL=rtsp://admin:your-camera-password@192.168.1.22:554/h264Preview_01_main

# === IMPORTANT: set the camera's RTSP stream to 2 fps ===
# The motion gate assumes the ring buffer fills at 2 fps and computes
# frame-trail offsets from webhook_offsets_seconds=(2, 4, 6, 8). At 15fps
# (camera default) the trail compresses to <2s of pre-event frames and
# the gate breaks. See README.md "RTSP frame rate" for details.
